bound-lock/1 about="The Lean proof reading executes the declared compiler against handed source bytes after image preparation. Its input identity includes all Lean sources, lean-toolchain, lakefile.toml, lake-manifest.json, both policy vectors and the selected reader implementation. It checks the compiler version/commit and every dependency revision and tracked worktree. A successful receipt means the declared 16 theorem audits and both negative causes passed. No dependencies are installed inside the reading. Native read/open counters distinguish execution from verified reuse. This proof place is separate from npm consumption: consumers verify portable historical readings without installing Lean. Compiler and cache preparation is reported separately, never charged to an existing proof-reader ceiling. Native reading uses the existing 25-second global limit, with the existing 65536-byte capture boundary. Changes to declared inputs reopen the reading; no prose claim closes it." at=witness:044/lean-kernel by=owner epoch=2 form=interval measure=count needs=proofs/lean/lean-toolchain|proofs/lean/lakefile.toml|proofs/lean/lake-manifest.json|proofs/lean/Obligations.lean|proofs/lean/Obligations/Cell.lean|proofs/lean/Obligations/Bridge.lean|proofs/lean/Obligations/HellyComb.lean|vectors/laws/meet-semilattice.json|vectors/laws/helly-comb.lean.json role=demands scope=publication/evidence/lean sig="ed25519:era1:v73cMsW77WnllJVzAPprJY67ZZOeKbM6FbWtBnKQ6ChBpUQyJHrqQgVpq3HU9hU6tClWsVOfHZUfW1LkBwXICA==" value=0..0
